#: DOĞRULAMA BEYANI — parti 39 (A3) Back-Massier-Gier (1964) turunun NİHAİ
#: cümlesi. Panel/uç bu çizgiden SAPAMAZ: "deneyle doğrulandı" HİÇBİR YERDE
#: ima edilmez. Metin ölçümün kendisidir, pazarlama değil.
#:
#: KÜNYE (KU-K6 / LULE-2b S2, 6 Eki 2026): metin "NASA TR 32-654" diyordu.
#: Ölçülen tapa tabloları o raporda DEĞİL: TR 32-654 (15 Eki 1964) konik
#: lülelerde duvar basıncı karşılaştırmasıdır ve B tabloları yoktur; tablolar
#: JPL (NASA değil) Technical Report 32-415 Rev. 1'dedir (15 Şub 1965;
#: veri kaydının kendi künyesi de bu, NTRS 19650010083). Yerel metinle
#: doğrulandı: ``HRMA-kaynaklar/metin-tur3/LULE-2b`` iki raporun kapak ve
#: sayfa başlıkları. "1964" yılı (dergi sürümü, LULE-2b notu; bu turda
#: dergi sayfası doğrulanmadı) ve uç sözleşmesindeki "Back, Massier &
#: Gier 1964" dizgisi korunur. TR 32-654'ün 27 Eki 1965 erratası (Denk. 4
#: ve 6) o raporun C_d / ses çizgisi bağıntısını kullanan yerin künyesidir;
#: bu cümle o bağıntıyı kullanmaz.
CFD_VISCOUS_VALIDATION_BASIS = (
    'VALIDATION STATUS, HONESTLY (measured 2026-08-19 against '
    'Back, Massier & Gier 1964, JPL Technical Report 32-415 Rev. 1 of '
    '15 Feb 1965, the repository\'s own '
    'digitised tap tables): the v3 CFD core REPRODUCES THE GEOMETRY AND '
    'THE CHOKED MASS FLOW of that nozzle - the as-built contour sits '
    'within 0.30% of the tap table from throat to exit and the solved mass '
    'flow lands in [0.989, 1.022] of the measured value in five of six '
    'runs, a band that is the experiment\'s own discharge-coefficient '
    'scatter. THE WALL HEAT FLUX IS NOT VALIDATED. The viscous+SA run '
    'destabilises as the first wall cell thins, so the wall-resolved grid '
    'the validation needs (y+ <~ 1, which is ni ~ 600-1200 in that case) '
    'was NOT REACHED. In the band that does settle (y+ ~ 27-42) the model '
    'UNDER-predicts q_w at the throat by a factor of 2-3, and the deficit '
    'closes systematically as y+ falls - i.e. it is a RESOLUTION result, '
    'not a model result, and a wall-integrating closure is not valid in '
    'that band to begin with. Therefore: q_w, h_g and the Bartz comparison '
    'below are published WITH THE y+ BADGE ATTACHED and nothing here may '
    'be read as "validated against experiment". Three cross-checks did '
    'close independently of the solver and are recorded in the repository: '
    'the Bartz cross-check (ratio band 1.45-2.68, monotone with pressure), '
    'the negative tests, and the ANSYS triple.')

